  `Ref[any]` is not Pekko's `ref ! PoisonPill`; **5c** (#1321) a stopped actor's dead letters are not published in mailbox order when
  Kill is queued between user messages (Go: `2, 3, 4, Kill`; Pekko: `2, Kill, 3, 4`). Each of those two is pinned by a test with a `TODO`.
  Not claimed: full parity, `gracefulStop` (#873), timers with a PoisonPill payload (#1191), Typed. Tests:
  [`poison_pill_test.go`](actor/poison_pill_test.go).
- **JVM `Error` and `InterruptedException` have no direct Go equivalent.** Pekko's default decider does not match a
  non-`Exception` `Throwable` (it is escalated, `FaultHandling.scala:210-217`) and handles `InterruptedException` apart
  (#450 item 5). The Go default decider (`DefaultStrategy`) is defined for every cause and **never returns Escalate**:
  a panic is a failure like any returned error (Restart), and `ErrGoexit` is a Go-only adaptation (Stop). A parent
  reaches Escalate only through its own decider. See [ADR 0017](../docs/adr/0017-supervision.md) S12.
- A directive outside `Resume`, `Restart`, `Stop` and `Escalate` fails the parent with `ErrInvalidDirective`; a
  decider panic fails the parent with `*PanicError`.
- A `Failed` is decided before user messages queued at the parent, one at a time, and is held while the parent is suspended.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["child Receive fails"] --> B{"parent declares a strategy?"}
    B -->|No| C["child stops"]
    B -->|Yes| D["child and its children suspended; Failed queued at the parent"]
    D --> E["decider(ctx, child, cause)"]
    E -->|Resume| F["child and subtree resumed"]
    E -->|Restart| J{"Budget allows?"}
    J -->|Yes| K["PreRestart(old), new instance, PostRestart"]
    J -->|No| G
    E -->|Stop| G["child stop accepted"]
    E -->|"Escalate or ok == false"| H["parent fails with the same cause"]
    E -->|"invalid directive or decider panic"| I["parent fails with ErrInvalidDirective or *PanicError"]
```

